/// Narrow shared borrow of the Store's FinalClaim V2 exposure edge.
///
/// The sibling funding wrappers are minted by a `const fn` that captures only
/// the Store. This one is deliberately different: it is minted by a validating
/// constructor and carries the three facts the exposure will be bound to. That
/// is the more fail-closed shape, and the reason is the window it closes —
/// `persist_verified_claim` takes only the capability, so a chain, an action
/// scope or a validation height accepted at persist time could differ from the
/// one that was validated. Carrying them here means the values proved at mint
/// time are the values used.
///
/// None of the four fields has an accessor. The wrapper has no `Clone`,
/// `Copy`, `Debug`, `Deref`, `AsRef`, codec or public constructor, and it
/// cannot recover the enclosing Store.
pub struct FinalClaimTransactionSinkRefV2<'store> {
    store: &'store ContractsSessionStoreV1,
    authorization: &'store ConsumedClaimSigningAuthorizationV2,
    chain_id: [u8; 32],
    action_scope_digest: [u8; 32],
    validation_height: u64,
}

/// Linear proof that one exact FinalClaim was exposed durably before any
